<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Guastalla</h1><p class="st-meta">1406 CE – 1748 CE · capital Guastalla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Po valley state first ruled by the Torelli and then by a branch of the Gonzaga, before joining Parma in 1748.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1406 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guido-torelli">Guido Torelli</a>, a condottiere in the service of the Visconti, received Guastalla, a town on the Po between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Parma</a>. The Torelli ruled it as counts under the overlordship of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Duchy of Milan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1539 Countess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovica-torelli">Ludovica Torelli</a> sold Guastalla to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrante-i-gonzaga">Ferrante Gonzaga</a>, general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and governor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>, whose branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> ruled it from then on. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrante-ii-gonzaga">Ferrante II</a> was made duke in 1621. The duchy was a fortified town with its farmland, and its rulers were often drawn into the quarrels over the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Duchy of Mantua</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Guastalla <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> died out in 1746. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-aachen">Aix-la-Chapelle</a> in 1748 the duchy was given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-duke-of-parma">Philip of Bourbon</a> and joined to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-guastalla.jpg" alt="Duchy of Guastalla" width="320" height="180"><figcaption>Image: Placide de Saint-Hélène · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duchies_of_Guastalla,_Bozzolo_and_Sabbioneta.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1406 CE – 1748 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guastalla</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Guido Torelli, Ferrante I Gonzaga, Ferrante II Gonzaga</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Guastalla, Guastalla</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1577&amp;focus=duchy-of-guastalla" aria-label="Duchy of Guastalla on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4934 591 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Guastalla lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5254 847L5229 694M5254 847L5246 851M5254 847L5250 844"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5246 851h0M5250 844h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5254 847h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5254 847h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guastalla. <a href="/atlas?year=1577&amp;focus=duchy-of-guastalla">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
